{"ts": 1789779103.335142, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "Best is f2+f10-f33 at 0.981, still below the 1.026 bar. The structure is very regular: triples of the top singles all land near 0.9\u20130.98, and there's no sign of a special interaction anywhere. That's an important diagnostic.\n\nLet me quantify it before deciding whether more search is worthwhile. If the features were independent with per-feature signal, an equal-weight combo of three signals with individual Sharpes s\u2081,s\u2082,s\u2083 would give roughly \u221a(s\u2081\u00b2+s\u2082\u00b2+s\u2083\u00b2). For {2,10,33}: \u221a(0.589\u00b2+0.580\u00b2+0.544\u00b2) = 0.99. Observed: 0.981. The additivity is almost exact across every triple I tested. There is no hidden interaction structure to discover \u2014 the features are essentially independent signal carriers, and combination gain is fully explained by diversification.\n\nThis tells me the ceiling. Let me confirm by checking a few combos the additive model predicts should be the very best, plus verify the model on a weak-feature control."}
